  "question": {
    "text": "Which among the following halide/s will not show <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math> reaction:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot3_0046_529d998c7859.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 149px;\"/>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot4_0046_37fc7c9f6b0b.png\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 174px;\"/>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Vinylic halides are organic compounds containing their halogen atom bonded to one of the two carbon atoms in the double bond present in that molecule.</p><p>Vinyl halide will not show <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math> reaction, due to very<br/>less stability of carbocation formed and partial<br/>double bond character in C — Cl bond.</p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo></mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is very unstable, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>=</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CH</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> cannot give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math> reaction.</p><p>Hence, the answer is B.</p>"
  }
